From 3a767e3893aecaec8ee328a011adb02df8d232e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] Play HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision has
 three values: off, where the display has no HDR10+, always

"Play HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision" sent an HDR10+ video as native Dolby
Vision only where the display takes Dolby Vision and not HDR10+. Many TVs
take both (Panasonic, Philips, TCL, Hisense), and some people prefer Dolby
Vision on them all the same. The setting now has three values
(videoscreen.hadesdvfromhdr10plusmode, DVBRIDGE::Hdr10PlusMode):

- Off, the default, unchanged.
- Where the display has no HDR10+: what "on" did, exactly.
- Always: also where the display takes HDR10+, by the user's preference.

Its help says what Always costs, in plain words: on a display that takes
HDR10+ the video's own HDR10+ is the more faithful picture, because the
studio's tone curve, target display and windows do not carry over to Dolby
Vision, so "Where the display has no HDR10+" is the recommended choice.
The choice of the video in "HDR output (this video)" still decides over
the setting.

The boolean of earlier builds (videoscreen.hadesdvfromhdr10plus) cannot be
read as an integer (CSettingInt::FromString() refuses "true" and Kodi keeps
the default), so it stays, hidden, and is taken over when the settings load,
as the other booleans with more values are (settings/SettingTakeOver.h):
true becomes "Where the display has no HDR10+", false or nothing stays off,
and while Kodi runs the boolean follows the setting (true for both values
that send HDR10+ as Dolby Vision), so an earlier build reads what it can do.
Nothing else names the boolean.

What sent an HDR10+ video as Dolby Vision to a display that takes HDR10+ is
decided with the reason why not (Hdr10PlusAsDolbyVisionOver(), on the same
facts as Hdr10PlusAsDolbyVisionWhy()). kodi.log says it once a video: for
Always, that it was sent as Dolby Vision by the setting although the display
takes HDR10+, and that its own HDR10+ would be the more faithful picture;
for the choice of the video, that it was chosen. The player information
says Always as a note ("Sent as Dolby Vision, as "Play HDR10+ videos as
Dolby Vision" (Always) asks, although this display takes HDR10+."), with
what to do ("Its own HDR10+ is more faithful here: choose "Where the display
has no HDR10+" ..."); the
reason "the display takes HDR10+" is given only with "Where the display has
no HDR10+". The line of the settings that change the picture from the film
counts both values that make a video Dolby Vision, with the same words
(PictureDefaults.h), and its button puts the setting back to off.

Strings: the label and the help keep their ids (60922, 60923; Estuary 52096,
52097); new: the value "Where the display has no HDR10+" (62877, Estuary
54968), the sentence (54969) and what to do (54970), in en_gb, es_es, es_ar
and es_mx. system/hades made again with make-playerinfo.py.
